{"id": "EUVD-2026-58989", "enisaUuid": "d29e89c2-8490-3da4-a6e9-54ce393e6581", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nata: libata-core: Add NOLPM quirk for PNY CS900 1TB SSD\n\nThe PNY CS900 1TB SSD (Phison PS3111-S11, DRAM-less) drops off the bus\nafter entering Device-Initiated Slumber during idle. With the default\nmed_power_with_dipm policy the link goes down (SStatus 1 SControl 300)\nand does not recover, forcing the filesystem read-only. Forcing\nmax_performance keeps the link stable across prolonged idle.\n\nAdd a NOLPM quirk so link power management is disabled for this drive\nspecifically, leaving it intact for other devices on the host.", "datePublished": "2026-08-15T05:51:53", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:44:19", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/eb94157a86cef9a151ccd4bc52faae1853d0fa0c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0a2c89d538fd4fca07c6ebe4fe03cc932f962441", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/299739909c486bcea7445f5c3b066fdbc0d2df96", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/462775c620197adaabc983ce847e5b9878ff4cb0"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-72031", "GHSA-hr25-grq7-6pp2"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1245afba-8f6b-3d50-b79e-60d005215353", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7627a0edef548c4c4dea62df51cc26bfe5bbcab8 <462775c620197adaabc983ce847e5b9878ff4cb0"}, {"id": "33485d7c-16d5-3655-b168-b6792c82095c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.5"}, {"id": "37ed721c-918c-33d6-89f1-0ebf78fcc531", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7627a0edef548c4c4dea62df51cc26bfe5bbcab8 <299739909c486bcea7445f5c3b066fdbc0d2df96"}, {"id": "4aaf2797-5b6e-3f3a-b94c-0644157ccf0d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7627a0edef548c4c4dea62df51cc26bfe5bbcab8 <0a2c89d538fd4fca07c6ebe4fe03cc932f962441"}, {"id": "62d2a5a0-3929-362e-b483-c24760ab0fe3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}, {"id": "7384405d-4012-3bd2-8f9e-1bf9c7fbfe92", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "a70eb9af-9532-3841-bff0-30c2e1f758a0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "b1df730b-1980-3bb3-be02-b1cdc79d2aa3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.9"}, {"id": "dcc34d6c-eda2-38be-a2e2-b733ddb14b0e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7627a0edef548c4c4dea62df51cc26bfe5bbcab8 <eb94157a86cef9a151ccd4bc52faae1853d0fa0c"}, {"id": "e9350d95-3032-3d54-806d-bffd45171cc3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.57"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "67109119-4508-3e01-af0c-ab4cd7aeb3b2", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}